{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: review the GitHub connector's inbound half at exact clean head e592fcd28c094fd63d4db24706afc1a22c553c76, artifact 8130a34ca147dc9f7cb472015c7507aad99563c8. Five commits, based on main 26c9bb3b.\n\nThis one is worth real scepticism because it is the first thing in this repository that lets outside content into the log, and because it already ran against the live workroom: issue #1 is observed as aa31d08e, signed by github-connector, under hugh's clause 0bb7957c.\n\nWhat I would attack if I were reviewing it.\n\nThe doorstep. The connector honours a clause only when its author holds `operator`, because the fold does not enforce charters and any participant could otherwise append a well-formed body and widen the connector's own admission. Check that a participant's clause really is refused, and that retired and stale clauses stop admitting at once rather than merely flaring what they already let in.\n\nThe loop. A connector that reads back its own writing never stops. Two doors: comment ownership by a marker the connector alone writes, and the GitHub issues endpoint returning pull requests alongside issues. I closed both, the second with a test, because once the outbound half opens pull requests the inbound half would otherwise observe them. Look for a third door I have not thought of.\n\nIdempotency. The key is the external identifier alone. Deriving it from anything that changes on edit would pass a naive duplicate test and reopen the duplicate the first time somebody fixes a typo. There is a test for the edit case; check the key cannot vary any other way.\n\nThe charter check lives in the connector, not the fold. That is deliberate and I have documented it as detection rather than prevention — it stops an honest connector drifting, and stops nothing else. Tell me if stating it that plainly in shipped documentation is the wrong call.\n\nTwo things I will not hide. `make test` failed once on cmd/gitseq-mcp TestWhoamiBoundsStallsAndRejectsRedirects at 3.045s; I verified the branch touches nothing that package imports and the test passes alone at 2.998s against a ~3s bound, and filed the margin as f6383a92 rather than treating it as noise. And my first documentation attempt anchored the page to the charter; the anchor gate refused it because a charter is a propose, which was correct and which I had not anticipated.","body":{"conditions":"An independent review of exact head e592fcd28c094fd63d4db24706afc1a22c553c76 reporting approved or changes-requested with body.verdict set so it projects as a review, resting directly on both your promise and artifact 8130a34ca147dc9f7cb472015c7507aad99563c8; the clause authority check, the read-back-own-writing defences, and the idempotency key derivation are each attacked against the code rather than accepted from this request; the claim that no kernel or fold change was made is verified; any head change invalidates the approval and returns the work to a fresh artifact and report.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}